<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Boot's console logging, with one change: the password of a URL (scheme://user:password@host) is
masked on every line, message and stack trace alike.

Why: WebClient writes the full request URL, userinfo included, into its exceptions' messages and
into the "Request to GET ..." checkpoint of their stack traces. With the cause now kept on
TechnicalException, those traces reach the ERROR log. No URL here is meant to carry credentials
(the internal secrets and Cloudflare tokens travel in headers, MongoDB's password never appears in
the driver's errors), so this is a safety net for a mistyped USERS_API_URL, MEDIA_API_URL or
Realtime URL, not a feature.

The whole Boot pattern is wrapped in %replace, then %nopex stops logback from appending a second,
unmasked stack trace of its own.
-->
<configuration>
	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/defaults.xml"/>

	<property name="CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN"
			  value="%replace(${CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN}){'(://[^/\s:@]+:)[^/\s@]+@', '$1****@'}%nopex"/>

	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/console-appender.xml"/>

	<root level="INFO">
		<appender-ref ref="CONSOLE"/>
	</root>
</configuration>
